IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`

-- Crimes Act 1914 (Commonwealth) -- sections 4B, 4D, 4E and 4F: pecuniary
-- penalties for natural persons and bodies corporate, penalties at the foot
-- of a provision, where a pecuniary penalty may be recovered, and the effect
-- of alterations in penalties.
--
-- Each rule answers MAYBE BOOLEAN. The conventions are those of the other
-- modules of this encoding: JUST TRUE where the text gives the result;
-- JUST FALSE where a "where", "if" or "unless" condition of the text fails or
-- where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where the text lists
-- without closing the list or does not speak. A rule whose conclusion is
-- itself a "does not" answers JUST FALSE when its condition holds and NOTHING
-- otherwise. A number the rule yields is a second function beside it.

§ `Crimes Act 1914 (Cth) ss 4B-4F: pecuniary penalties`

§§ `Section 4B(1): bodies corporate as well as natural persons`

-- src:4372 | (1) A provision of a law of the Commonwealth relating to indictable offences or summary offences shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be deemed to refer to bodies corporate as well as to natural persons.
@ref s 4B(1) (src:4372)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth relating to indictable offences or summary offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4B(1) a provision is deemed to refer to bodies corporate as well as to natural persons` IS
    IF NOT `the provision is a provision of a law of the Commonwealth relating to indictable offences or summary offences`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 4B(2) and (2A): a pecuniary penalty for a natural person`

-- src:4373 | (2) Where a natural person is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth punishable by imprisonment only, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case, impose, instead of, or in addition to, a penalty of imprisonment, a pecuniary penalty not exceeding the number of penalty units calculated using the formula:
@ref s 4B(2) (src:4373)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is punishable by imprisonment only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4B(2) the court may impose a pecuniary penalty instead of, or in addition to, imprisonment` IS
    IF NOT (`the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` AND `the offence is punishable by imprisonment only`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The most the penalty may be: the number of penalty units calculated using
-- the formula (sidecar entry s 4B(2): Term of Imprisonment x 5), where
-- the rule above says the court may impose one.
-- src:4373 | (2) Where a natural person is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth punishable by imprisonment only, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case, impose, instead of, or in addition to, a penalty of imprisonment, a pecuniary penalty not exceeding the number of penalty units calculated using the formula:
-- src:4374 | where:
-- src:4375 | Term of Imprisonment is the maximum term of imprisonment, expressed in months, by which the offence is punishable.
@ref s 4B(2) (src:4373-4375)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is punishable by imprisonment only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum term of imprisonment` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4B(2) the number of penalty units the pecuniary penalty may not exceed` IS
    IF `s 4B(2) the court may impose a pecuniary penalty instead of, or in addition to, imprisonment` `the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` `the offence is punishable by imprisonment only` `a contrary intention appears` `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `the number of penalty units calculated using the formula` `the maximum term of imprisonment`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4376 | (2A) Where a natural person is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth in respect of which a court may impose a penalty of imprisonment for life, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case, impose, instead of, or in addition to, a penalty of imprisonment, a pecuniary penalty not exceeding 2,000 penalty units.
@ref s 4B(2A) (src:4376)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court may impose a penalty of imprisonment for life for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4B(2A) the court may impose a pecuniary penalty instead of, or in addition to, imprisonment for life` IS
    IF NOT (`the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` AND `a court may impose a penalty of imprisonment for life for the offence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4376 | (2A) Where a natural person is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth in respect of which a court may impose a penalty of imprisonment for life, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case, impose, instead of, or in addition to, a penalty of imprisonment, a pecuniary penalty not exceeding 2,000 penalty units.
@ref s 4B(2A) (src:4376)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court may impose a penalty of imprisonment for life for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4B(2A) the number of penalty units the pecuniary penalty may not exceed` IS
    IF `s 4B(2A) the court may impose a pecuniary penalty instead of, or in addition to, imprisonment for life` `the person is a natural person convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` `a court may impose a penalty of imprisonment for life for the offence` `a contrary intention appears` `the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the number of penalty units for an offence punishable by imprisonment for life`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4B(3) and (3A): a pecuniary penalty for a body corporate`

-- src:4377 | (3) Where a body corporate is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks fit, impose a pecuniary penalty not exceeding an amount equal to 5 times the amount of the maximum pecuniary penalty that could be imposed by the court on a natural person convicted of the same offence.
@ref s 4B(3) (src:4377)
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4B(3) the court may impose a pecuniary penalty on a body corporate` IS
    IF NOT `the person is a body corporate convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the court thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4377 | (3) Where a body corporate is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks fit, impose a pecuniary penalty not exceeding an amount equal to 5 times the amount of the maximum pecuniary penalty that could be imposed by the court on a natural person convicted of the same offence.
@ref s 4B(3) (src:4377)
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum pecuniary penalty that could be imposed by the court on a natural person convicted of the same offence, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4B(3) the number of penalty units the pecuniary penalty on a body corporate may not exceed` IS
    IF `s 4B(3) the court may impose a pecuniary penalty on a body corporate` `the person is a body corporate convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` `a contrary intention appears` `the court thinks fit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`the amount equal to 5 times the natural person's maximum` `the maximum pecuniary penalty that could be imposed by the court on a natural person convicted of the same offence, in penalty units`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4378 | (3A) Where an Act (whether enacted before or after the commencement of this subsection) confers power to make an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws but not including a law of a Territory) and specifies the maximum pecuniary penalty that can be imposed for offences created by such an instrument, then:
-- src:4379 | (a) unless the contrary intention appears, the specified penalty is taken to be the maximum penalty that the instrument can prescribe for such offences by natural persons; and
@ref s 4B(3A)(a) (src:4378-4379)
GIVEN `an Act confers power to make an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a law of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act specifies the maximum pecuniary penalty that can be imposed for offences created by such an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4B(3A)(a) the specified penalty is taken to be the maximum penalty that the instrument can prescribe for such offences by natural persons` IS
    IF NOT (`an Act confers power to make an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws)` AND (NOT `the instrument is a law of a Territory`) AND `the Act specifies the maximum pecuniary penalty that can be imposed for offences created by such an instrument`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4378 | (3A) Where an Act (whether enacted before or after the commencement of this subsection) confers power to make an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws but not including a law of a Territory) and specifies the maximum pecuniary penalty that can be imposed for offences created by such an instrument, then:
-- src:4379 | (a) unless the contrary intention appears, the specified penalty is taken to be the maximum penalty that the instrument can prescribe for such offences by natural persons; and
-- src:4380 | (b) where a body corporate is convicted of such an offence—the specifying of that penalty is not to be treated as an indication of a contrary intention for the purposes of applying subsection (3).
@ref s 4B(3A)(b) (src:4378-4380)
GIVEN `an Act confers power to make an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a law of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act specifies the maximum pecuniary penalty that can be imposed for offences created by such an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a body corporate is convicted of such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4B(3A)(b) the specifying of the penalty is treated as an indication of a contrary intention for the purposes of applying subsection (3)` IS
    IF `an Act confers power to make an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws)` AND (NOT `the instrument is a law of a Territory`) AND `the Act specifies the maximum pecuniary penalty that can be imposed for offences created by such an instrument` AND `a body corporate is convicted of such an offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4B(4): payment to a person aggrieved`

-- src:4381 | (4) Where under a law of the Commonwealth any forfeiture, penalty or reparation is paid to a person aggrieved, it is payable to a body corporate where the body corporate is the person aggrieved.
@ref s 4B(4) (src:4381)
GIVEN `a forfeiture, penalty or reparation is paid to a person aggrieved under a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is the person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4B(4) the forfeiture, penalty or reparation is payable to the body corporate` IS
    IF `a forfeiture, penalty or reparation is paid to a person aggrieved under a law of the Commonwealth` AND `the body corporate is the person aggrieved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 4D: penalties at the foot of a provision`

-- Where a penalty is printed. A penalty at the foot of a subsection that is
-- also at the foot of the section containing it is at the foot of a section, so
-- the position is four facts: at the foot of a section, of a subsection, of a
-- clause of a Schedule, or of a subclause.
DECLARE FootPosition HAS
    `at the foot of a section of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the foot of a subsection of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the foot of a clause of any Schedule to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the foot of a subclause of any Schedule to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:4396 | (1A) Subsection (1) applies to a penalty set out:
-- src:4397 | (a) at the foot of a section of an Act; or
-- src:4398 | (b) at the foot of a subsection of an Act, but not at the foot of the section containing the subsection; or
-- src:4399 | (c) at the foot of a clause of any Schedule to an Act; or
-- src:4400 | (d) at the foot of a subclause of any Schedule to an Act, but not at the foot of the clause containing the subclause.
@ref s 4D(1A) (src:4396-4400)
GIVEN `the position` IS A FootPosition
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4D(1A) subsection (1) applies to a penalty set out` IS
    IF     `the position`'s `at the foot of a section of an Act`
        OR (`the position`'s `at the foot of a subsection of an Act` AND (NOT `the position`'s `at the foot of a section of an Act`))
        OR `the position`'s `at the foot of a clause of any Schedule to an Act`
        OR (`the position`'s `at the foot of a subclause of any Schedule to an Act` AND (NOT `the position`'s `at the foot of a clause of any Schedule to an Act`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4393 | (1) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a penalty, whether pecuniary or otherwise, set out at the foot of any provision of an Act as described in a paragraph of subsection (1A) indicates:
-- src:4394 | (a) if the provision expressly creates an offence—that the offence is punishable on conviction by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out; or
@ref s 4D(1)(a) (src:4393-4394)
GIVEN `the position` IS A FootPosition
      `the provision expressly creates an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4D(1)(a) the offence is punishable on conviction by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out` IS
    IF `s 4D(1A) subsection (1) applies to a penalty set out` `the position` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE IF `the provision expressly creates an offence` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4393 | (1) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a penalty, whether pecuniary or otherwise, set out at the foot of any provision of an Act as described in a paragraph of subsection (1A) indicates:
-- src:4394 | (a) if the provision expressly creates an offence—that the offence is punishable on conviction by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out; or
-- src:4395 | (b) in any other case—that contravention of the provision is an offence against the provision, punishable on conviction by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.
@ref s 4D(1)(b) (src:4393-4395)
GIVEN `the position` IS A FootPosition
      `the provision expressly creates an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4D(1)(b) contravention of the provision is an offence against the provision, punishable on conviction by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out` IS
    IF `s 4D(1A) subsection (1) applies to a penalty set out` `the position` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE IF `the provision expressly creates an offence` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "not exceeding the penalty so set out": the two numbers are in the same
-- unit (penalty units, months of imprisonment or dollars).
-- src:4393 | (1) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a penalty, whether pecuniary or otherwise, set out at the foot of any provision of an Act as described in a paragraph of subsection (1A) indicates:
-- src:4394 | (a) if the provision expressly creates an offence—that the offence is punishable on conviction by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out; or
-- src:4395 | (b) in any other case—that contravention of the provision is an offence against the provision, punishable on conviction by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.
@ref s 4D(1) (src:4393-4395)
GIVEN `the penalty imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalty set out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4D(1) a penalty is not exceeding the penalty so set out` IF
    `the penalty imposed` AT MOST `the penalty set out`

DECLARE ProvisionOfSection4B IS ONE OF
    `subsection 4B(2)`
    `subsection 4B(2A)`
    `subsection 4B(3)`
    `another provision`

-- src:4401 | (1B) Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of subsection 4B(2), (2A) or (3).
@ref s 4D(1B) (src:4401)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A ProvisionOfSection4B
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4D(1B) subsection (1) affects the operation of` IS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `another provision` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:4402 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to any instrument made under an Act (including rules, regulations or by-laws but not including a law of a Territory) as if the instrument were an Act and as if each such rule, regulation or by-law were a section of an Act.
@ref s 4D(2) (src:4402)
GIVEN `it is an instrument made under an Act (including rules, regulations or by-laws)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a law of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4D(2) subsection (1) applies to the instrument` IS
    IF `it is a law of a Territory`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is an instrument made under an Act (including rules, regulations or by-laws)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4402 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to any instrument made under an Act (including rules, regulations or by-laws but not including a law of a Territory) as if the instrument were an Act and as if each such rule, regulation or by-law were a section of an Act.
@ref s 4D(2) (src:4402)
GIVEN `it is a rule, regulation or by-law made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a law of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4D(2) the rule, regulation or by-law is treated as a section of an Act` IS
    IF `it is a law of a Territory`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is a rule, regulation or by-law made under an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4E: recovery in a court of summary jurisdiction`

-- src:4404 | A pecuniary penalty for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth may, unless the contrary intention appears, be recovered in any court of summary jurisdiction.
@ref s 4E (src:4404)
GIVEN `it is a pecuniary penalty for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is a court of summary jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4E the pecuniary penalty may be recovered in the court` IS
    IF NOT `it is a pecuniary penalty for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the court is a court of summary jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4F: effect of alterations in penalties`

-- src:4406 | (1) Where a provision of a law of the Commonwealth increases the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence, the penalty or maximum penalty as increased applies only to offences committed after the commencement of that provision.
@ref s 4F(1) (src:4406)
GIVEN `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth increases the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement of that provision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4F(1) the penalty or maximum penalty as increased applies to the offence` IS
    IF NOT `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth increases the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `an offence was committed after the commencement` `the day of the offence` `the day of commencement of that provision`

-- src:4407 | (2) Where a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence, the penalty or maximum penalty as reduced extends to offences committed before the commencement of that provision, but the reduction does not affect any penalty imposed before that commencement.
@ref s 4F(2) (src:4407)
GIVEN `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement of that provision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4F(2) the penalty or maximum penalty as reduced extends to an offence committed before the commencement` IS
    IF NOT `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `an offence was committed before the commencement` `the day of the offence` `the day of commencement of that provision`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4407 | (2) Where a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence, the penalty or maximum penalty as reduced extends to offences committed before the commencement of that provision, but the reduction does not affect any penalty imposed before that commencement.
@ref s 4F(2) (src:4407)
GIVEN `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the penalty was imposed` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement of that provision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4F(2) the reduction affects a penalty imposed before the commencement` IS
    IF NOT `a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `a penalty was imposed before the commencement` `the day the penalty was imposed` `the day of commencement of that provision`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING
